CORE
main.c
--function f --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A --function harness substitutes earlier nondeterministic arguments into a
runtime static minimum and allocates a valid variable-length argument array.
The instantiated precondition at the harness call must be present and hold.
